{"id":"G0092","name":"TA505","aliases":["Hive0065","Spandex Tempest","CHIMBORAZO"],"url":"https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0092","summary":"TA505 is a cyber criminal group that has been active since at least 2014. TA505 is known for frequently changing malware, driving global trends in criminal malware distribution, and ransomware campaigns involving Clop.","summaryCites":[{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Sep 2017","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/threat-actor-profile-ta505-dridex-globeimposter"},{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 June 2018","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/ta505-shifts-times"},{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Jan 2019","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/servhelper-and-flawedgrace-new-malware-introduced-ta505"}],"procedures":[{"id":"T1027.002","text":"TA505 has used UPX to obscure malicious code.","cites":[{"name":"IBM TA505 April 2020","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200420201624/https://securityintelligence.com/posts/ta505-continues-to-infect-networks-with-sdbbot-rat/"}]},{"id":"T1027.010","text":"TA505 has used base64 encoded PowerShell commands.","cites":[{"name":"Cybereason TA505 April 2019","url":"https://www.cybereason.com/blog/threat-actor-ta505-targets-financial-enterprises-using-lolbins-and-a-new-backdoor-malware"},{"name":"Deep Instinct TA505 Apr 2019","url":"https://www.deepinstinct.com/blog/new-servhelper-variant-employs-excel-4-0-macro-to-drop-signed-payload"}]},{"id":"T1027.013","text":"TA505 has password-protected malicious Word documents.","cites":[{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Sep 2017","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/threat-actor-profile-ta505-dridex-globeimposter"}]},{"id":"T1055.001","text":"TA505 has been seen injecting a DLL into winword.exe.","cites":[{"name":"IBM TA505 April 2020","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200420201624/https://securityintelligence.com/posts/ta505-continues-to-infect-networks-with-sdbbot-rat/"}]},{"id":"T1078.002","text":"TA505 has used stolen domain admin accounts to compromise additional hosts.","cites":[{"name":"IBM TA505 April 2020","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200420201624/https://securityintelligence.com/posts/ta505-continues-to-infect-networks-with-sdbbot-rat/"}]},{"id":"T1112","text":"TA505 has used malware to disable Windows Defender through modification of the Registry.","cites":[{"name":"Korean FSI TA505 2020","url":"https://www.fsec.or.kr/user/bbs/fsec/163/344/bbsDataView/1382.do?page=1&column=&search=&searchSDate=&searchEDate=&bbsDataCategory="}]},{"id":"T1140","text":"TA505 has decrypted packed DLLs with an XOR key.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group TA505","url":"https://research.nccgroup.com/2020/11/18/ta505-a-brief-history-of-their-time/"}]},{"id":"T1218.007","text":"TA505 has used `msiexec` to download and execute malicious Windows Installer files.","cites":[{"name":"Cybereason TA505 April 2019","url":"https://www.cybereason.com/blog/threat-actor-ta505-targets-financial-enterprises-using-lolbins-and-a-new-backdoor-malware"},{"name":"Deep Instinct TA505 Apr 2019","url":"https://www.deepinstinct.com/blog/new-servhelper-variant-employs-excel-4-0-macro-to-drop-signed-payload"},{"name":"Trend Micro TA505 June 2019","url":"https://blog.trendmicro.com/trendlabs-security-intelligence/shifting-tactics-breaking-down-ta505-groups-use-of-html-rats-and-other-techniques-in-latest-campaigns/"}]},{"id":"T1218.011","text":"TA505 has leveraged `rundll32.exe` to execute malicious DLLs.","cites":[{"name":"Cybereason TA505 April 2019","url":"https://www.cybereason.com/blog/threat-actor-ta505-targets-financial-enterprises-using-lolbins-and-a-new-backdoor-malware"},{"name":"Deep Instinct TA505 Apr 2019","url":"https://www.deepinstinct.com/blog/new-servhelper-variant-employs-excel-4-0-macro-to-drop-signed-payload"}]},{"id":"T1553.002","text":"TA505 has signed payloads with code signing certificates from Thawte and Sectigo.","cites":[{"name":"Cybereason TA505 April 2019","url":"https://www.cybereason.com/blog/threat-actor-ta505-targets-financial-enterprises-using-lolbins-and-a-new-backdoor-malware"},{"name":"Deep Instinct TA505 Apr 2019","url":"https://www.deepinstinct.com/blog/new-servhelper-variant-employs-excel-4-0-macro-to-drop-signed-payload"},{"name":"Trend Micro TA505 June 2019","url":"https://blog.trendmicro.com/trendlabs-security-intelligence/shifting-tactics-breaking-down-ta505-groups-use-of-html-rats-and-other-techniques-in-latest-campaigns/"}]},{"id":"T1553.005","text":"TA505 has used.iso files to deploy malicious.lnk files.","cites":[{"name":"TrendMicro TA505 Aug 2019","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/19/h/ta505-at-it-again-variety-is-the-spice-of-servhelper-and-flawedammyy.html"}]},{"id":"T1685","text":"TA505 has used malware to disable Windows Defender.","cites":[{"name":"Korean FSI TA505 2020","url":"https://www.fsec.or.kr/user/bbs/fsec/163/344/bbsDataView/1382.do?page=1&column=&search=&searchSDate=&searchEDate=&bbsDataCategory="}]},{"id":"T1583.001","text":"TA505 has registered domains to impersonate services such as Dropbox to distribute malware.","cites":[{"name":"Korean FSI TA505 2020","url":"https://www.fsec.or.kr/user/bbs/fsec/163/344/bbsDataView/1382.do?page=1&column=&search=&searchSDate=&searchEDate=&bbsDataCategory="}]},{"id":"T1588.001","text":"TA505 has used malware such as Azorult and Cobalt Strike in their operations.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group TA505","url":"https://research.nccgroup.com/2020/11/18/ta505-a-brief-history-of-their-time/"}]},{"id":"T1588.002","text":"TA505 has used a variety of tools in their operations, including AdFind, BloodHound, Mimikatz, and PowerSploit.","cites":[{"name":"NCC Group TA505","url":"https://research.nccgroup.com/2020/11/18/ta505-a-brief-history-of-their-time/"}]},{"id":"T1608.001","text":"TA505 has staged malware on actor-controlled domains.","cites":[{"name":"Korean FSI TA505 2020","url":"https://www.fsec.or.kr/user/bbs/fsec/163/344/bbsDataView/1382.do?page=1&column=&searc