ence/shifting-tactics-breaking-down-ta505-groups-use-of-html-rats-and-other-techniques-in-latest-campaigns/"}]},{"id":"T1059.005","text":"TA505 has used VBS for code execution.","cites":[{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Sep 2017","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/threat-actor-profile-ta505-dridex-globeimposter"},{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 June 2018","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/ta505-shifts-times"},{"name":"Trend Micro TA505 June 2019","url":"https://blog.trendmicro.com/trendlabs-security-intelligence/shifting-tactics-breaking-down-ta505-groups-use-of-html-rats-and-other-techniques-in-latest-campaigns/"}]},{"id":"T1059.007","text":"TA505 has used JavaScript for code execution.","cites":[{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Sep 2017","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/threat-actor-profile-ta505-dridex-globeimposter"},{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 June 2018","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/ta505-shifts-times"}]},{"id":"T1106","text":"TA505 has deployed payloads that use Windows API calls on a compromised host.","cites":[{"name":"Korean FSI TA505 2020","url":"https://www.fsec.or.kr/user/bbs/fsec/163/344/bbsDataView/1382.do?page=1&column=&search=&searchSDate=&searchEDate=&bbsDataCategory="}]},{"id":"T1204.001","text":"TA505 has used lures to get users to click links in emails and attachments. For example, TA505 makes their malware look like legitimate Microsoft Word documents,.pdf and/or.lnk files.","cites":[{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Sep 2017","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/threat-actor-profile-ta505-dridex-globeimposter"},{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 June 2018","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/ta505-shifts-times"},{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Jan 2019","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/servhelper-and-flawedgrace-new-malware-introduced-ta505"}]},{"id":"T1204.002","text":"TA505 has used lures to get users to enable content in malicious attachments and execute malicious files contained in archives. For example, TA505 makes their malware look like legitimate Microsoft Word documents,.pdf and/or.lnk files.","cites":[{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Sep 2017","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/threat-actor-profile-ta505-dridex-globeimposter"},{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 June 2018","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/ta505-shifts-times"},{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Jan 2019","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/servhelper-and-flawedgrace-new-malware-introduced-ta505"}]},{"id":"T1559.002","text":"TA505 has leveraged malicious Word documents that abused DDE.","cites":[{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 June 2018","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/ta505-shifts-times"}]},{"id":"T1552.001","text":"TA505 has used malware to gather credentials from FTP clients and Outlook.","cites":[{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Sep 2017","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/threat-actor-profile-ta505-dridex-globeimposter"}]},{"id":"T1555.003","text":"TA505 has used malware to gather credentials from Internet Explorer.","cites":[{"name":"Proofpoint TA505 Sep 2017","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/threat-insight/post/threat-actor-profile-ta505-dridex-globeimposter"}]},{"id":"T1069","text":"TA505 has used TinyMet to enumerate members of privileged groups. TA505 has also run `net group /domain`.","cites":[{"name":"IBM TA505 April 2020","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200420201624/https://securityintelligence.com/posts/ta505-continues-to-infect-networks-with-sdbbot-rat/"},{"name":"Trend Micro TA505 June 2019","url":"https://blog.trendmicro.com/trendlabs-security-intelligence/shifting-tactics-breaking-down-ta505-groups-use-of-html-rats-and-other-techniques-in-latest-campaigns/"}]},{"id":"T1087.003","text":"TA505 has used the tool EmailStealer to steal and send lists of e-mail addresses to a remote server.","cites":[{"name":"Trend Micro 